WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.310
Say you're building a writing app.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:03.830
Every save keeps a revision,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.620
so writers can go back to any earlier version.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.540
You ask your coding agent

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.410
to keep that history small.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.370
Seconds later, a nightly job deletes old revisions.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.470
The agent writes down what the job does:

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.610
a hard delete.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.770
But revisions are append-only,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.410
and that trait forbids hard deletes for good.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.380
The check fails.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.420
So the agent adds a grant for it.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.180
Still blocked: no grant overrides a final forbid.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.890
It marks the effects unknown instead.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.680
That fails too: unknown is never read as none.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.230
Deleting revision history is a decision for people.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.750
Change the rule in the model, with the code,

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:43.710
and review it.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.270
Shape checks the claims against each other.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.910
The pull request's review, by a teammate,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.650
a CI job or a review agent,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.830
checks them against the code.
